{"authored" [{"question" "q-81031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $v=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}]$\nthat corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-\\sqrt{2}\\text{i},$\nthen what is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\,\\lambda =-\\sqrt{2}\\text{i},$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2}\\text{i} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{2}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2+\\sqrt{2}\\text{i} & 2 \\\\ -3 & -2+\\sqrt{2}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the homogeneous system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}(2+\\sqrt{2}\\text{i}){x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+(-2+\\sqrt{2}\\text{i}){x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the matrix $A-(-\\sqrt{2}\\text{i})I$ is singular, the system above must have a non-zero solution. This means that one equation of the system is a multiple of another. As a result, we can drop one of the rows and take one of the variables to be the free variable. For example, from the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}(2+\\sqrt{2}\\text{i}){x}_{1}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}(2+\\sqrt{2}\\text{i}){x}_{1}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{1}\\in C.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{1}=-2,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2+\\sqrt{2}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{-2}{2+\\sqrt{2}\\text{i}}=\\frac{-2(2-\\sqrt{2}\\text{i})}{6}=-\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0aed9f2d60c3511e84d5ff8866713509b9d5a365e5d992dfbf6afbb654d9a514" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "fi